  "label": "Legal Inspection of Religious Attire",
  "description": "The concept that law enforcement may or may not be permitted to inspect religious attire, such as the niqab, under specific legal frameworks. This involves constitutional rights, privacy laws, and religious freedom statutes. In some jurisdictions, such inspections may be deemed unconstitutional or illegal if they infringe on personal liberties or religious expression.",
